# H96 Max V58: freeze Mesa at the Panthor-compatible build.
#
# Open Panthor GPU stack on this box only works with the kisak Mesa build
# (26.1.4~kisak1~r). Stock/newer Mesa does not drive Mali-G610 Panthor here,
# and a broken GPU stack on a TV box means no picture, indistinguishable
# from a dead box to anyone using it.
#
# h96-gaming-setup.sh force-installs these exact versions, but is Type=oneshot
# guarded by /var/lib/h96-gaming-setup-done: it runs once, then never again.
# With no hold and no pin, the next apt upgrade (or Discover) pulls a newer
# Mesa and nothing puts it back.
#
# Priority >1000 is deliberate: it forces apt to keep this exact version even
# when a newer one is available, which normal pinning (<=1000) would not do.
Package: libgl1-mesa-dri mesa-vulkan-drivers libglx-mesa0 libegl-mesa0 libgbm1 mesa-libgallium libglapi-mesa mesa-va-drivers mesa-vdpau-drivers
Pin: version 26.1.4~kisak1~r*
Pin-Priority: 1001
